From 34e9af915839756f1ada2ee39a9e59b74c925928 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Huang <sebastian_huang@accton.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:06:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: refresh the MediaTek SDK kernel patches for 6.12.94

The SDK kernel patches were made for kernel 6.12.74 without the TIP
mediatek patches. On 6.12.94 with the TIP patches, 9 of them did not
apply and one applied in the wrong function. Refresh them:

- 999-dual-boot-02: drop. 971-kernel-boot-param-and-dual-image-rootfs
  already adds the same no_default_rootdev option.
- 999-eth-46: drop. The fix is in 6.12.94.
- 999-dual-boot-01: refresh, it applied with fuzz.
- 999-ephy-i2p5g-03: apply on top of the rcu_stall workaround for
  the MT7988 2.5G PHY and restore the SDK's locked PDOWN write. The
  SDK kernel config does not build this driver.
- 999-eth-33: merge the SDK MTU handling in mtk_change_mtu() with the
  PPE MTU update added in 6.12.x.
- 999-ppe-08, 999-ppe-28, 999-ppe-39: refresh for context changed in
  6.12.x (mtk_ppe_update_mtu(), mtk_flow_is_valid_idev()).
- 999-ppe-29: the IPsec push block applied to flow_offload_work_stats()
  because flow_offload_encap_tunnel() now returns int. Move it into
  flow_offload_encap_tunnel() and check flow_action_entry_next() for
  NULL like the code around it.
- 999-crypto-04, 999-eth-09, 999-eth-32, 999-eth-38, 999-pcie-02,
  999-wed-11: refresh, they applied with fuzz. The hunks were checked
  to land in the intended functions.

The SDK patches now apply without fuzz and the kernel builds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
